[{:db/id 17592186162067 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-10f2f9d4-7d62-5e91-afc7-8a268909f88f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162277 :question/problem "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.75$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[3X+2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.2+2\\cdot 0.3+3\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.2+4\\cdot 0.3+9\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =5.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.9-{2.3}^{2} \\\\  & =0.61.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =1.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+4\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =3.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =3.25-{1.75}^{2} \\\\  & =0.1875.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-2Y] & ={3}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & ={3}^{2}(0.61)+{2}^{2}(0.1875) \\\\  & =6.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158864 :answer-field/correct 17592186158866 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162062 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e466b3e6-da95-5e08-8c31-060b08be1979" "question-4592eee9-4d66-541e-b103-0104f487a3d0" "question-4ebe566e-595e-53c5-acba-b32f38c7b929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e466b3e6-da95-5e08-8c31-060b08be1979" :question/id #uuid "e466b3e6-da95-5e08-8c31-060b08be1979" :question/math-academy-id "q-129524" :question/problem "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=3$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=1.$ Find $\\text{Var}[6X+4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[6X+4Y]={6}^{2}\\cdot 3+{4}^{2}\\cdot 1=124.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9075f10-8356-5116-9d8d-9363c1194e5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9075f10-8356-5116-9d8d-9363c1194e5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9075f10-8356-5116-9d8d-9363c1194e5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b313ad8e-b7ae-5e7c-b6c7-5711116d766f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cdf6d31-4ecc-5d71-be94-0e1394489376" "answer-61bb06c0-eefd-5dd5-9a60-e0cb63bc7e4a" "answer-b313ad8e-b7ae-5e7c-b6c7-5711116d766f" "answer-62e4e3c6-27ff-5891-9e8d-1d5f6c4b8e3b" "answer-6bca8e49-1df7-5904-85a2-f8689d1b6976"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cdf6d31-4ecc-5d71-be94-0e1394489376" :answer/id #uuid "6cdf6d31-4ecc-5d71-be94-0e1394489376" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "102" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61bb06c0-eefd-5dd5-9a60-e0cb63bc7e4a" :answer/id #uuid "61bb06c0-eefd-5dd5-9a60-e0cb63bc7e4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "112" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b313ad8e-b7ae-5e7c-b6c7-5711116d766f" :answer/id #uuid "b313ad8e-b7ae-5e7c-b6c7-5711116d766f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62e4e3c6-27ff-5891-9e8d-1d5f6c4b8e3b" :answer/id #uuid "62e4e3c6-27ff-5891-9e8d-1d5f6c4b8e3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bca8e49-1df7-5904-85a2-f8689d1b6976" :answer/id #uuid "6bca8e49-1df7-5904-85a2-f8689d1b6976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4592eee9-4d66-541e-b103-0104f487a3d0" :question/id #uuid "4592eee9-4d66-541e-b103-0104f487a3d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129525" :question/problem "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=100$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=200.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X+0.4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X+0.4Y]={0.5}^{2}\\cdot 100+{0.4}^{2}\\cdot 200=57.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d483090b-1213-58fe-9189-e5ba9f5e3d4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d483090b-1213-58fe-9189-e5ba9f5e3d4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "d483090b-1213-58fe-9189-e5ba9f5e3d4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1028e093-da26-54ef-aa43-a9f56a4e0493" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19ab9ab2-922f-5d8d-a24b-0e98ec213cd4" "answer-c9397ba9-a60b-592b-a489-b40297be8dd6" "answer-d3eb23d5-5f09-5681-8d44-ab8a69f5b550" "answer-1028e093-da26-54ef-aa43-a9f56a4e0493" "answer-0bbc9a21-53ce-5107-963d-75a23a6b47c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19ab9ab2-922f-5d8d-a24b-0e98ec213cd4" :answer/id #uuid "19ab9ab2-922f-5d8d-a24b-0e98ec213cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "130" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9397ba9-a60b-592b-a489-b40297be8dd6" :answer/id #uuid "c9397ba9-a60b-592b-a489-b40297be8dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3eb23d5-5f09-5681-8d44-ab8a69f5b550" :answer/id #uuid "d3eb23d5-5f09-5681-8d44-ab8a69f5b550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "507" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1028e093-da26-54ef-aa43-a9f56a4e0493" :answer/id #uuid "1028e093-da26-54ef-aa43-a9f56a4e0493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "57" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bbc9a21-53ce-5107-963d-75a23a6b47c8" :answer/id #uuid "0bbc9a21-53ce-5107-963d-75a23a6b47c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "83" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4ebe566e-595e-53c5-acba-b32f38c7b929" :question/id #uuid "4ebe566e-595e-53c5-acba-b32f38c7b929" :question/math-academy-id "q-129526" :question/problem "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=20$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y]={(0.5)}^{2}\\cdot 20+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 5=25.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f087f72-105f-5680-aa6c-80acf118c1cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f087f72-105f-5680-aa6c-80acf118c1cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f087f72-105f-5680-aa6c-80acf118c1cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9dd32b7a-4ad9-58cc-91f9-9026f1bd2828" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a5a011e-bc53-5bc4-8f45-39b4c9f6a5b6" "answer-ee19091b-a43a-5af6-af43-e22fe399a03b" "answer-d66b4a53-dbb5-5db6-b6ce-d24df3369ea2" "answer-97641fd2-bedb-53d0-a380-c9fdb8513014" "answer-9dd32b7a-4ad9-58cc-91f9-9026f1bd2828"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a5a011e-bc53-5bc4-8f45-39b4c9f6a5b6" :answer/id #uuid "1a5a011e-bc53-5bc4-8f45-39b4c9f6a5b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee19091b-a43a-5af6-af43-e22fe399a03b" :answer/id #uuid "ee19091b-a43a-5af6-af43-e22fe399a03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d66b4a53-dbb5-5db6-b6ce-d24df3369ea2" :answer/id #uuid "d66b4a53-dbb5-5db6-b6ce-d24df3369ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97641fd2-bedb-53d0-a380-c9fdb8513014" :answer/id #uuid "97641fd2-bedb-53d0-a380-c9fdb8513014" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9dd32b7a-4ad9-58cc-91f9-9026f1bd2828" :answer/id #uuid "9dd32b7a-4ad9-58cc-91f9-9026f1bd2828" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-10f2f9d4-7d62-5e91-afc7-8a268909f88f" :question/id #uuid "10f2f9d4-7d62-5e91-afc7-8a268909f88f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129540" :question/problem "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=8,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=11$\nand second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=70$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=130.$ Find the variance of  $4X-\\frac{1}{3}Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =70-{8}^{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =130-{11}^{2} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4X-\\frac{1}{3}Y] & ={4}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =16\\cdot 6+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e537044c-a663-5a85-97de-b5e333853075"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e537044c-a663-5a85-97de-b5e333853075" :answer-field/id #uuid "e537044c-a663-5a85-97de-b5e333853075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-34df106a-01bf-52c7-8732-4b94b3d12e4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7e27671-31ae-5207-9120-d8a7d847ed6f" "answer-2ede9d25-89b7-5e8f-9713-24a9987fd2b8" "answer-f52d6a13-0e5e-5a4a-a0e1-bd443e